			"body": "A phaser gives a sound a slow, swirling motion. Frequency places the sweep, depth sets how far it\\ntravels and rate how fast. With feedback low the effect is gentle; turned up it becomes a pronounced,\\nwhistling resonance. It suits pads, chords and hi-hats.",
